l with a decisive financial advantage, having raised $3.6 million and holding $1.8 million on hand, while Democrat Dwayne Romero has raised about $717,000 with limited cash remaining. Minor-party and independent candidates are also on the ballot.\n\nThe race has drawn attention as competitive: the lone public poll from July showed a one-point contest, and Hurd has campaigned on his disagreements with Trump while touting disaster-relief work on the Western Slope. Most expert raters call the race Likely Republican, with several at Lean Republican and one at Tossup. Prediction markets give Romero roughly a one-in-three chance, consistent with a Republican favorite but a real contest.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.2665, "margin": -3.72}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.3144, "margin": -3.5}]}